// spec: STM-002
//
// A declaration may not be the body of a branch or a loop.  It used to be
// accepted, and the name ESCAPED into the enclosing scope -- so whether it
// existed was decided by a runtime condition.
//
// ⚠️ Fixing this REMOVED a compiler divergence rather than creating one: the C
// back end already refused the construct (C-12), so the language, the compiler
// and the interpreter now agree.

if True then var X := 1;
